part e1_gifts
  tally 2
  note "E1-03: gifts and inheritances across the family. Halina's gifts to Ania are A's (a.acq, a.gift_tax; A/gift.tally); Zbigniew's estate and its tax are D's (d.igt_tax, d.igt_arises, d.report_by; D/estate.tally). E1 adds only what neither states: that Halina gave from her own property, so nothing she gave Ania was part of Zbigniew's estate. Whether Anna, Piotr and Jakub reported their inheritance no paper says (story.md 2025-05-05): the two cases are scenarios (scenarios/e1_reported.tally, scenarios/e1_not_reported.tally)."

index e1_gift = [cash2021, units2023]
  note "Halina's gifts to Ania, by A's keys of acq: the 15 000.00 DUK in cash of 2021-04-30 (A-D19) and the 200 BRZ-GLB-A units of 2023-09-12 (A-D18)"

input e1_gift_own[g in e1_gift]: bool question "Did Halina give this from her own property, outside the community with Zbigniew (CIV-1 .3)?"

def e1_gifts_in_estate: bool
  note "whether any of Halina's gifts to Ania came out of what became Zbigniew's estate: the estate is his own property and his half of the community (CIV-2 .2), so a gift of Halina's own property (CIV-1 .3) is no part of it; D-D07 .1 lists no fund units among what she takes from the estate"
  rule base = any(not e1_gift_own[g] for g in e1_gift)

version e1_gift_cash
  cite e1_story
  governs always
  known 2021-04-30
  e1_gift_own[cash2021] = true "story.md 2021-04-30: from the money she inherited from her mother in 2018 (her own); CIV-1 .3: what a spouse acquires by inheritance is her own"

version e1_gift_units
  cite e1_story
  governs always
  known 2023-09-12
  e1_gift_own[units2023] = true "story.md 2023-09-12: Halina had bought them with her own money; CIV-1 .3: what a spouse acquires in exchange for her own assets is her own"
